\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Modular components of BO. Each frame is a component whose options can be exchanged. The interfaces between components are the predictive distribution of the surrogate and the acquisition function, so in principle any option in one frame can be combined with the options in the others. The trust region restricts the search of the acquisition optimizer.}}{8}{figure.caption.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces Computation of expected improvement for minimization with (a) a Gaussian process and (b) TabPFN. The shaded region marks values below the best observation $y_n^*$. A GP gives a Gaussian posterior of $f(\boldsymbol {x})$, for which the expectation has a closed form. TabPFN gives a predictive distribution of $y$ over bins of unequal width, with constant density in the interior bins and half-normal outer tails, and the expectation is obtained by summing the contribution $e_k$ of each bin weighted by its probability $p_k$. The shapes are schematic.}}{16}{figure.caption.7}%
